+## Dev9 — v0.3 spectral-integrity falsification methods
+
+Dev9 advances the open catalogue from 180 to **183 methodologies** by consuming Audio Spectral Integrity v0.3 without copying its DSP. It adds WOLA/local complementary bucket views, a strict exact-reference oracle-template qualification method, and a blinded four-condition control-trial generator.
+
+The new methods are deliberately falsification-oriented. WOLA exists to test whether conclusions survive local-window rather than full-clip FFT filtering. The oracle refuses unknown audio because exact A/B references are mandatory. The blind trial keeps its condition key private until free-transcription/source-count responses are locked. None of these methods establishes source separation, recovered transcript truth, playback location or intent.
+
+The v0.2 five-method line remains available with unchanged methodology IDs; the provider dynamically imports the v0.3 upstream implementation and records its source hash. See `spec/AUDIO_SPECTRAL_INTEGRITY_METHODS.md`.
+
 ## Dev8 — spectral-integrity lineages, revision lifecycle and compute planning
 
 Dev8 grows the open catalogue from 175 to **180 methodologies** by importing five bounded methods from Audio Spectral Integrity v0.2: complementary alternating-bucket views, bucket-origin phase sensitivity, bounded preference listening views, externally seeded harmonic observations, and the known two-input interleave positive control.  These methods preserve the upstream rule that odd/even bucket views split one captured waveform and are **not source separation**.
