 # Audio Spectral Integrity methods
 
-Media Methodologies dev8 consumes **Audio Spectral Integrity v0.2** as a provider-neutral experimental backend.  The provider remains the owner of the transforms; this package owns only methodology registration, applicability, execution profiles, experiment lineage and provenance glue.
+Media Methodologies dev9 consumes **Audio Spectral Integrity v0.3** as a provider-neutral experimental/falsification backend. The provider remains the owner of the transforms; this package owns methodology registration, applicability, execution profiles, experiment lineage and provenance glue.
 
-The methods are intentionally plural and bounded:
+The v0.2 methods remain unchanged:
 
-- `AUDIO.SPECTRAL_INTEGRITY.COMPLEMENTARY_BUCKET_VIEWS` creates complementary odd/even alternating spectral views from **one** captured waveform.  Their exact recombination inside the selected passband is a transform identity, not evidence that the recording contained two physical sources.
-- `AUDIO.SPECTRAL_INTEGRITY.PHASE_SWEEP` repeats the partition at predeclared bucket origins and measures how strongly conclusions depend on arbitrary mask boundaries.
-- `AUDIO.SPECTRAL_INTEGRITY.BOUNDED_PREFERENCE_VIEW` attenuates the non-preferred bucket set and peak-scales the result.  It is a derived listening candidate and adds no information.
-- `AUDIO.SPECTRAL_INTEGRITY.HARMONIC_OBSERVATION` measures expected-harmonic support only when an independent `f0` hypothesis is supplied.  It does not infer speaker identity or a second source.
-- `QUAL.AUDIO.SPECTRAL_INTERLEAVE_POSITIVE_CONTROL` constructs a mathematically known two-input spectral weave.  Only this controlled fixture has known per-bucket source ownership.
+- `AUDIO.SPECTRAL_INTEGRITY.COMPLEMENTARY_BUCKET_VIEWS` creates full-clip complementary odd/even alternating spectral views from **one** captured waveform. Their exact passband recombination is a transform identity, not evidence that the recording contained two physical sources.
+- `AUDIO.SPECTRAL_INTEGRITY.PHASE_SWEEP` shifts bucket origins and measures sensitivity to arbitrary mask boundaries.
+- `AUDIO.SPECTRAL_INTEGRITY.BOUNDED_PREFERENCE_VIEW` creates a peak-safe derived listening candidate by attenuation only.
+- `AUDIO.SPECTRAL_INTEGRITY.HARMONIC_OBSERVATION` measures expected-harmonic support only when an independent `f0` hypothesis is supplied.
+- `QUAL.AUDIO.SPECTRAL_INTERLEAVE_POSITIVE_CONTROL` constructs a mathematically known two-input spectral weave.
+
+Dev9 adds the three v0.3 falsification/qualification paths:
+
+- `AUDIO.SPECTRAL_INTEGRITY.WINDOWED_BUCKET_VIEWS` uses sqrt-Hann WOLA windows to localise bucket-filter ringing in time. It is deliberately compared against the full-clip FFT method. At a Nyquist ceiling, odd+even must reconstruct the source within numerical tolerance; below Nyquist it reconstructs the declared WOLA-bandlimited view.
+- `QUAL.AUDIO.SPECTRAL_ORACLE_TEMPLATE_PROJECTION` requires the **exact known A and B reference waveforms plus the known mixture**. It fits A/B coefficients independently in odd/even bucket regions. This is a controlled oracle and is unavailable for unknown field audio.
+- `QUAL.AUDIO.SPECTRAL_BLIND_CONTROL_TRIAL` creates anonymous single-A, notched-single-A, ordinary-A+B and engineered-weave controls. The condition key is private and must stay outside public source control until free-transcription/source-count responses are locked.
 
 ## Scientific boundary
 
-Field results may support statements about the declared transform, bucket energy, phase sensitivity, recombination error or externally seeded harmonic support.  They do not by themselves establish words, speakers, source count, emitters, intent, a historical multiplexing process, or criminal conduct.
+Field results may support statements about the declared transform, bucket energy, origin/window sensitivity, recombination error or externally seeded harmonic support. They do not by themselves establish words, speakers, source count, emitters, intent, a historical multiplexing process, or criminal conduct.
+
+The oracle and blind-control methodologies are **known-input qualification only**. Their success cannot be transferred to an unknown recording without an independent held-out classifier/decision rule and natural/codec/room/loudspeaker controls. A notched single voice remains a first-class false-positive control.
 
-All transformed streams remain derived material.  Originals and immutable source references must be retained separately.  Blind listening notes are observations about listeners, not an automatic semantic label on the source waveform.
+All transformed streams remain derived material. Originals and immutable source references must be retained separately. Blind listening notes are observations about listeners, not automatic semantic labels on the source waveform.
